Why two licenses?

Code in this repository (everything under `src/`, plus example scripts and
configuration) is licensed under Apache-2.0 (see LICENSE). The written
taxonomy is licensed under CC BY 4.0 because attribution is the point: this
is a body of patterns meant to be cited, restated, and built on. If you use
a pattern from the catalogue in a talk, a paper, a blog post, or your own
agent framework, credit keeps the lineage legible for everyone who follows.

